{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Second review-plan run → BLOCK on P4 (oversize), then remediated\n\nThe re-run BLOCKED on a single **deterministic** criterion **P4 (oversize)**: `description is 9220 chars (> 8000)`. Crucially `llm_ran: None` — this fast-failed on the deterministic floor, so it consumed **ZERO Bedrock** (no LLM G-criteria ran). Cause: my previous description revision (adding the pinned pydantic-ai 1.107.2 source detail + the Option B mechanism narration) pushed it over `verify.max_ticket_description_chars` (8000). NOT a design/substantive objection.\n\nRemediated per P4's own suggested_fix — moved the proof narration into these comments and trimmed the description to the reader-essential problem/constraints/acceptance-criteria/testing. Description is now **6650 chars** (1350 under the cap). The plan is gate-ready.\n\nNote for the record: on the FIRST run the LLM G-criteria DID run and produced **no substantive/design blocking finding** — its only block was f4ae (plan-text clarity: \"how does the leg marker reach the exception the predicate inspects\"), now fully documented, plus advisory f626 which drove the Option B refactor. So the design already cleared the LLM's substantive review once.\n\nHolding for operator authorization before consuming another LLM gate run (a successful re-run now proceeds past P4 into the ~15–20 min Bedrock G-criteria)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788056094583698048,"uuid":"67639c63-82d5-4d08-b0eb-b6a301997661"}